From 4928956b08081ac5f8c4b397504541bfa0493aa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:10:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] video: rzg2l: play however many frames are installed

The intro length was LOGO_FRAMES_DEFAULT, a compiled-in 4 that the
payload had to match: install fewer and every boot printed a load error
and a "cut to N frames" warning; install more and the extra ones were
never shown.  Replacing the artwork meant rebuilding the bootloader and
re-flashing fip, for what is really a property of the rootfs.

Load frame 00, 01, ... until the next file does not exist.  Presence is
checked with file_exists() first, so the normal end of the intro is
silent instead of an ext4load error.  "logo_frames" in the environment
still caps the count; with a cap set, a missing frame is reported as
before, since then it is one the user asked for.  The upper bound is the
room between LCD_SRCM_ADDR and the display list headers, as it already
was.

Frame 0 now gets its full share of the screen.  It goes up with the
pipeline and used to stay only while the other frames loaded - a couple
of hundred milliseconds - and then the chain moved straight on to frame
1, so the first picture was visibly shorter than the rest.  The chain
now starts with however many more output frames frame 0 needs to reach
logo_rate_ms, counted from when the pipeline started.  The header budget
check accounts for it.

The default pace comes from RZG2L_LOGO_RATE_MS, which the Yocto layer
sets from RZG3L_LOGO_SEQUENCE_RATE_MS, and is 1000 ms when built on its own:
one second a frame, as in the RZ/G2L PoC this intro replaces.
"logo_rate_ms" overrides it at run time as before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G3L boot logo, board specific]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
